/data/
/out/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/

# THE GENERATED WEB DATA IS TRACKED, and it is the only generated thing that is.
#
# `data/` and `out/` stay ignored: they are hundreds of megabytes and some of the sources
# (Orphanet CC BY-ND, the Human Protein Atlas CC BY-SA) are not ours to redistribute. But
# that means no CI runner can rebuild the site's numbers from a clone, and a published
# explorer with no data is not a publication. So the converted JSON under web/ is committed
# — 4.5 MB, the artefacts themselves — and the deploy workflow says plainly that it is
# publishing them rather than reproducing them.
#
# The ignore rules above are ANCHORED (`/data/`, not `data/`) for that reason: unanchored,
# they matched web/src/data and web/public/data as well, and no negation can un-ignore a
# file inside an ignored directory.

# LaTeX build artefacts (generated/numbers.tex IS tracked - it is the audit trail)
paper/build/
*.aux
*.bbl
*.bcf
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.log
*.out
*.run.xml
*.synctex.gz
*.toc

# Ingested public catalogues: large, versioned by their publishers, and some are
# not redistributable (Orphanet CC BY-ND, HPA CC BY-SA). Fetch with tools/ingest.py.
/data/ontology/

# Assistant working directories. Session state, skill caches and scratch files: local to
# one machine and one person, and not part of the method this repository publishes.
.claude/
.claude*/
**/.claude/
CLAUDE.md
